{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And now, write for yourselves this song</b> — on the level of peshat, He commands both Moses and Joshua to write it, for He wished to make Joshua a prophet during Moses' lifetime. Now Moses wrote it, and Joshua stood beside him, reading and seeing. This is the sense of 'So Moses wrote' (Deuteronomy 31:22). <b>and teach it to the children of Israel</b> — this refers to Moses, for he is the principal one, since from him they will hear and learn. For Joshua too was teaching alongside him, as it says at the end, 'he and Hoshea the son of Nun' (Deuteronomy 32:44). And the sense of <b>this song</b> is: the song that I am now about to declare to you, namely Ha'azinu. It is called a song because Israel will recite it continually in song and melody, and so too it was written in the format of a song, for songs are written with breaks at the places of the melody."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:32.786906499Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}